    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57b7b6b5_646d8340",
        "filename": "chip/g/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 388,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-20T21:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a pretty big implicit assumption of ordering. It\u0027d be better if there was no assumption and you ensured other_image made sense -- or get rid of it entirely and just pass a pointer into curreng_image_is_newer() to get the other image. You could just call it here again. It shouldn\u0027t be an issue, and there\u0027s no longer any assumptions that can be broken with ordering if something changes in the future.\n\n\nint current_image_is_newer(struct SignedHeader **other_image)\n{\n   ...\n\n   if (other_image !\u003d NULL)\n    *other_image \u003d other;\n   return 0;\n}\n\nint system_rollback_detected(void)\n{\n  return !!current_image_is_newer(NULL);\n}\n\nint system process_retry_counter(void)\n{\n  struct SignedHeader *other_image;\n  \n  ...\n \n  if (current_image_is_newer(\u0026other_image)) {\n     ...\n  }\n  corrupt_header(other_image);\n}",
      "parentUuid": "57b7b6b5_091dc0d8",
      "revId": "b1d15d9e78a74bf19905180de296fcf770f0cf4b",
